<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton market closed for local holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton market closed for local holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) was closed on Tuesday for a local religious holiday. It will reopen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The KCA's official spot rate for New Crop NIAB-78 closed 55 rupees up at 2,673 per maund (37.32 KG) on Monday. K-68 closed unchanged at 2,508 rupees and MNH-93 at 2,563.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
